  "scope": "Original application appearance runtime/default builders, append/equipment resolution, binding skins, dye conversion, filtering and ordered mutex/cycle propagation. Original configuration postprocessing for ID ranges, blacklist/whitelist and profession inheritance. Protocol-only models retain all data fields; network wrappers/serialization and unrelated item metadata are not ported.",
  "adaptations": [
    "Explicit per-service table context replaces global parsers; one resolver retains its scratch collections.",
    "Unity JSON payload projects dictionaries into ordered pairs and nested integer arrays into range wrappers, then reconstructs the original runtime dictionaries before original PostParse methods.",
    "Config row fields are mutable for Unity JSON deserialization; Luban byte constructors are replaced by the verified extraction.",
    "No SDK implementation is read, executed or incorporated. SpineSkinInfo is an application configuration record."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Not yet connected to the actual local player, native actor or profession prefab.",
    "Random appearance creation, network DTOs, general item parsers and player snapshot cloning are outside this port."
  ],
  "validated_scope": "Passed actual Direct3D Play Mode with the packaged current configuration: all 62 sex/profession default appearances; every blacklist/whitelist set and ordered inherited allowed list against an independent Python projection; real mage preview body and compatible/incompatible equipment, absent/zero secondary-weapon, bound skin, HSV, reused pool, ordered mutual/cycle/one-way/white-list and null-target branches. No UI or production character render was exercised."
}
